      "side": 1,
      "message": "Restricting the repair to conversations removed by this very fixStructures pass would defeat the purpose: the inconsistency is historical, not produced by the current run. The comment a few lines above already documents exactly this class of damage: \"On oldest version, removeConversation didn\u0027t update appdata/contacts causing a potential incorrect state between appdata/contacts and appdata/convInfos\". In the case that motivated this patch the conversation had been erased more than a year before, by an older version, and unlinkConversations() cleared the conversationId with nothing ever setting it again.\n\nOn the invariant itself: removeConversation() (handleNewConversation) already recreates a one-to-one conversation for every contact that pointed at the conversation being removed, unconditionally and with no extra filter. So the daemon already treats \"an active contact owns a one-to-one conversation\" as an invariant; this change simply restores it for contacts where it was lost. I deliberately kept the same condition as that existing path rather than adding a divergent one.\n\nBanned contacts are excluded: getContacts(false) does return them (the filter is !isActive() \u0026\u0026 !includeRemoved \u0026\u0026 !isBanned()), and isActive() screens them out here.",
      "parentUuid": "628e4746_7ec1af90",
