      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T19:56:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This cannot surface old messages: the conversation is created a few lines above, so its last commit is the initial commit of a brand new repository. There is no prior history to replay.\n\nAlso, sendMessageNotification() is not a chat-message notification. It announces a git commit (MIME_TYPE_GIT, {id, commit, deviceId}) to our other devices and to the conversation members. It is precisely how the peer learns that the conversation exists and can clone it. Dropping it would make the repair purely local: the contact would be visible again on this device but the peer would never be told, which is the opposite of the intent.\n\nThis mirrors the sendNotification() call that removeConversation() already performs after recreating a one-to-one conversation. Note that startConversation() only emits ConversationReady and syncs our own devices via needsSyncingCb_, so it does not cover the peer.",
